# Cursor Rules for E-Learning React Project

## Project Overview
This is an e-learning platform built with React, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS.

## Code Standards
- Use TypeScript for all components and utilities
- Follow React functional components with hooks
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Implement proper error handling and loading states
- Use meaningful variable and function names
- Add proper TypeScript types for all props and data

## File Structure
- Components should be in `/src/components/`
- Pages should be in `/src/pages/`
- Types should be in `/src/types/`
- Services should be in `/src/services/`
- Utils should be in `/src/utils/`

## Quiz System Requirements
- Quiz questions should be integrated into lessons, not separate pages
- Questions should appear after video completion
- Support multiple question types: multiple choice, true/false, fill in the blank
- Tutor can create and manage quiz questions for their courses
- Student progress should be tracked per lesson

## Component Guidelines
- Use proper prop interfaces
- Implement responsive design
- Add loading and error states
- Use consistent naming conventions
- Keep components focused and reusable

## State Management
- Use Redux Toolkit for global state
- Keep local state in components when appropriate
- Use proper TypeScript types for state

## Testing
- Write unit tests for utility functions
- Test component rendering and user interactions
- Mock external dependencies properly
